Use the NativeFunctionArrayGenerator tool to generate or update the arrays for games.

Create a new unit for each game, and edit the array so that the OperatorPrecedence
for the "&&", "||", "^^" operators is decreased to a value smaller than that of
any other operator so that they will have parenthesis around their operands
when that operands are other operators.

For example, the functions:

    {0018}(Index: 00130; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 030; Name: '&&'), // Core.u (ut436)
    {0019}(Index: 00131; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 030; Name: '^^'), // Core.u (ut436)
    {0020}(Index: 00132; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 032; Name: '||'), // Core.u (ut436)

must be modified to show these precedences:

    {0018}(Index: 00130; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 010; Name: '&&'), // Core.u (ut436)
    {0019}(Index: 00131; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 010; Name: '^^'), // Core.u (ut436)
    {0020}(Index: 00132; Format: nffOperator; OperatorPrecedence: 011; Name: '||'), // Core.u (ut436)

And remember the RegisterNativeFunctionArray call in the initialization section of the unit.
